{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And Moshe said: Who am I — whoever wishes to grasp the true plain sense of these verses will find understanding in this commentary of mine, for the earlier authorities before me did not understand it at all. Moshe responded to two things that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: to go to Pharaoh, and also to bring the Children of Israel out by Pharaoh's command. And Moshe responded to each one in turn." "Who am I, that I should go to Pharaoh — even to bring him a gift and a present? Am I even worthy to enter the court of a foreign king like me?!" "And that I should bring the Children of Israel out of Egypt — that is: even if I am worthy to enter before Pharaoh, I am a fool for the rest. What plausible thing could I say to him? Is Pharaoh a fool, to listen to me and send a great people who are his slaves out of his land for free?! And what plausible thing could I say to him, such that through that word I would bring them out of Egypt with Pharaoh's authorization?! And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him each in turn and said:"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:18.693985983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}